{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,320p' reviews/P48-general-lattice-projection-tower-closeout.md; printf '\\\\n--- P47 predecessor review ---\\\\n'; sed -n '1,180p' reviews/P47-center-finite-projection-core-closeout.md; printf '\\\\n--- semantic audit tail ---\\\\n'; tail -n 180 work/FORMALIZATION-SEMANTIC-AUDIT.md; printf '\\\\n--- decision tail ---\\\\n'; tail -n 180 work/FORMALIZATION-AUDIT-DECISION.md\"","aggregated_output":"# P48 closeout review — general-lattice local-code projection tower\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: proved at the stated conditional Lane-G scope; queue may advance.**\n\nThe completed Aristotle project was downloaded as `aristotle_responses/P48-general-lattice-projection-tower.tar.gz` (SHA-256 `fc7fa4031a4b93f21ca49f4041f75e6312cdf1b9a7122a111affee04f588a0f2`) and extracted, without building or fetching dependencies, at `aristotle_responses/P48-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p48-48zqafp9_aristotle/`.\n\nOnly the packet-authorized module `AristotleCandidates/GeneralLatticeProjectionTower.lean` was integrated into the live project. Its SHA-256 is `190af007e460f439360a0e195c6458e23f0aa5146009cb7f6b40ece2ea6b2386` in both the quarantine snapshot and live project. The archive and extraction remain as raw response records.\n\n## Exact declarations and assumptions\n\nFor a complex Hilbert space, the module defines `ProjectionTower.IsDecreasingProjTower`, `limitSpace`, and `ProjectionTower.limitProj (p : Nat -> H ->L[Complex] H) := (limitSpace p).starProjection`. The key abstract theorems are `IsDecreasingProjTower.tendsto_limitProj` and `IsDecreasingProjTower.limitProj_mem_vonNeumannAlgebra`.\n\nThe general-lattice declarations are `LocalCode.SupportSystem`, `LocalCode.LatticeExhaustion`, `LocalCode.stageSubgroup`, `LocalCode.latticeCodeProj`, and `LocalCode.latticeLimitProj`. The packet gate is discharged by `latticeCodeProj_mul_of_le`, `tendsto_latticeLimitProj`, `latticeLimitProj_mem_vonNeumannAlgebra`, and `latticeLimitProj_apply_of_invariant`.\n\nThe load-bearing assumptions are explicit: finite increasing stages exhausting the region; support behavior under unit, multiplication, and inverse; the local-finiteness instance `[forall n, Fintype (stageSubgroup E ss n)]`; a representation `U : S ->* (H ->L[Complex] H)` satisfying `forall g, star (U g) = U g^-1`; membership of all stage projections in the concrete von Neumann algebra; and invariance of the vector under each stage constraint. No convergence, normality, trace, or finiteness premise is hidden. The strong limit is proved internally. The listed local-finiteness, representation, membership, and invariance data remain auxiliary assumptions for the manuscript-facing conditional form.\n\n## Acceptance review\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | Under its explicit hypotheses, P48 constructs the decreasing local-code tower and its limiting projection `q`, proves pointwise strong convergence, `q` membership in the supplied concrete von Neumann algebra, and `q` fixing the supplied invariant vector. |\n| partial | The manuscript specialization remains conditional: local finiteness, the concrete GNS representation, stage membership in the intended regional algebra, and cyclic-vector invariance are interfaces, not derived from `main.tex:1026-1195`. |\n| blocked | Nothing blocks P48 at its gate. Corner traces, faithfulness/normality, finiteness/fullness of `q`, and central type-III exclusion are deferred to P49--P51. |\n| failed | None. |\n\nThe changed route is explicit: inclusion of finite stabilizer subgroups gives monotonicity of the group-average projections. This replaces the manuscript's partial-trace route and introduces no tensor-factor or local-hyperbolic premise. The stated mathematical target is met exactly at this conditional scope.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** P48, Lane G.\n- **Predecessors:** none. It imports only supporting theory `FiniteStabilizerProjector` and `BicommutantVonNeumannCore`, and no P47--P61 package.\n- **Permitted gate:** discharged: the decreasing general-lattice local-code projections and their limiting projection `q`, with exact conditional data, are available in the live project.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected. No corner trace, faithfulness, normality, finiteness, fullness, global weight, factor/type-III conclusion, hyperbolic basis, or tensor-factor coordinate claim occurs.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.GeneralLatticeProjectionTower` — passed.\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.CenterFiniteProjectionCore AristotleCandidates.GeneralLatticeProjectionTower Formalization` — passed.\n- `lake build` — passed in the already-built live project.\n- `lake env lean /dev/stdin` with `#print axioms` for the key convergence, monotonicity, membership, and invariance theorems — each reports only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- Placeholder/forbidden-declaration scan — no `sorry`, `admit`, user `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`, `implemented_by`, or `native_decide` occurrence.\n- Quarantine/live SHA-256 comparison and `git diff --check` — passed.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nNo acceptance-blocking finding. The audit checked that support closure suffices for stage subgroups, the finite-cardinal inversion is guarded by non-emptiness of a subgroup, the limiting projection is onto the intersection of fixed spaces, and all later Lane-G conclusions remain absent. Compilation validates the Lean terms, not the unformalized manuscript specialization hypotheses.\n\n## Cleanup and worktree state\n\nKept intentionally: the integrated P48 candidate, its quarantine archive and extraction, and this review. All pre-existing modified and untracked work was preserved. No manuscript file was changed; no commit, push, dependency update, archive build, or dependency fetch was performed.\n\n--- P47 predecessor review ---\n# P47 closeout review — center and finite-projection core\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: proved at the stated infrastructure scope; queue may advance.**\n\nThe completed Aristotle project was downloaded as\n`aristotle_responses/P47-center-finite-projection-core.tar.gz` (SHA-256\n`51640368062f659201ebae314966a1220fab89b20fa2dfa3c33e4ab364744ea6`) and\nextracted, without building or fetching dependencies, at\n`aristotle_responses/P47-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p47-80u8nxnx_aristotle/`.\nOnly the packet-authorized module\n`AristotleCandidates/CenterFiniteProjectionCore.lean` was integrated into the\nlive project.  Its SHA-256 is\n`c55831ac16d3dec3d471c25c24159a5c22c79dff1460c586830eadda27da57d8` in both\nthe quarantine snapshot and live project.  The archive and extraction remain\nas raw response records.\n\n## Exact declarations and assumptions\n\nFor a concrete `M : VonNeumannAlgebra H`, with\n`[NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H]`, the module\ndefines:\n\n- `center`, `IsProjection`, `IsCentralProjection`, and `ProjLe`;\n- `MvNEquiv`, `MvNLe`, and `IsFiniteProjection`;\n- the non-unital compressed algebra `corner`;\n- `IsCentralSupport` as a predicate and `IsFull := IsCentralSupport _ _ 1`.\n\nThe key checked lemmas are `coe_center`, `mem_center_iff`,\n`ProjLe.trans`, `MvNEquiv.trans`, `MvNEquiv.add`, `MvNLe.trans`,\n`IsFiniteProjection.mul_central`, `corner_eq_image`,\n`central_corner_eq_image`, `IsCentralSupport.unique`,\n`IsFull.mul_ne_zero`, `isFull_iff_forall_central`, and\n`IsFull.exists_nonzero_projection`.\n\nNo auxiliary mathematical premise was added.  The only imported project-local\ntheory is the already locally used P36 concrete bicommutant core\n`AristotleCandidates.BicommutantVonNeumannCore`; P47 imports no P47--P61\nsuccessor.  The compression/comparison proofs use the ambient C*-identity for\nbounded operators, not a topology, normality, or factor-classification\nassumption.\n\n## Acceptance review\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | The requested concrete algebraic vocabulary and basic center, order, compression, Murray--von Neumann comparison, finite-central-compression, central-support, and fullness lemmas.  In particular, `IsFull.mul_ne_zero` proves that a full projection meets every nonzero central projection nontrivially. |\n| partial | None within P47's stated algebraic target. |\n| blocked | Existence/construction of a central-support projection, projection-tower limits, normality, corner traces, and analytic comparison theory remain for later packets.  `IsCentralSupport` is intentionally only a predicate. |\n| failed | None. |\n\nP47's mathematical target is met at its stated scope.  It does **not** establish\na manuscript theorem, a finite corner for a particular projection, or a\nno-type-III conclusion.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** P47, Lane G.\n- **Predecessors:** none.  The packet-authorized P36 bicommutant import is\n  already locally present and compiled; it is supporting infrastructure, not\n  a P47--P61 dependency.\n- **Permitted gate:** discharged: the algebraic center/corner/fullness\n  vocabulary required by Lane G is available in the live project.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected.  The module contains no\n  projection tower, trace/state, global weight, fullness assertion for a\n  manuscript projection, type-III exclusion, normality, spatial tensor\n  factorization, or factor classification.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.CenterFiniteProjectionCore` — passed.\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.BicommutantVonNeumannCore AristotleCandidates.CenterFiniteProjectionCore Formalization` — passed.\n- `lake build` — passed in the already-built live project.\n- `lake env lean /dev/stdin` with `#print axioms` for\n  `IsFull.mul_ne_zero`, `IsFiniteProjection.mul_central`, `MvNLe.trans`,\n  `MvNEquiv.add`, `IsCentralSupport.unique`, `center`, and `corner` — each\n  reports only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- Placeholder/forbidden-declaration scan of P47 and its direct project import\n  — no `sorry`, `admit`, user `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`, `implemented_by`,\n  or `native_decide` occurrence.\n- Quarantine/live SHA-256 comparison and `git diff --check` — passed.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nNo acceptance-blocking finding.  The audit verified that the only generic\nfullness conclusion is the conditional algebraic intersection lemma, and that\nthe finite-compression theorem is not combined with it to claim the Lane-G/P51\ncentral finite-projection conclusion.  Residual mathematical risk is limited\nto the explicitly deferred analytic and existence results above; compilation\ndoes not validate those later claims.\n\n## Cleanup and worktree state\n\nKept intentionally: the integrated P47 candidate, its quarantine archive and\nextraction, and this review.  All pre-existing modified and untracked work was\npreserved.  No manuscript file was changed; no commit, push, dependency\nupdate, archive build, or dependency fetch was performed.\n\n--- semantic audit tail ---\n\n## Dependency spine and one-to-one theorem anchors\n\n### 1. Finite coordinate map\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> Given finite adapted source and target word bases, send each source word to a\n> phase-corrected target word.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nFiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarData.starEquiv\nFiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarData.starEquiv_word\nFiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarData.starEquiv_correctedWord\n```\n\nSemantic status: the construction is proved from the fields of\n`FiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarData`, but the actual manuscript-specific finite\ndata are not constructed from `main.tex:1671-1679` or `main.tex:1915-1920`.\n\n### 2. Coherence of finite maps\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> The finite coordinate maps commute with the inclusions of stages.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nstarEquiv_connecting_of_pauliBasis\nDirectedFiniteCoordinateFamily.stageEquiv_connecting\n```\n\nSemantic status: proved when word, label, phase, and connecting-map\ncompatibility are supplied.\n\n### 3. Algebraic infinite map\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> Compatible finite maps descend to a unique star-isomorphism of algebraic\n> direct limits.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nDirectedFiniteCoordinateFamily.alpha\nDirectedFiniteCoordinateFamily.alpha_of\nDirectedFiniteCoordinateFamily.existsUnique_alpha\n```\n\nSemantic status: this is a genuine algebraic direct-limit theorem, conditional\non the finite coherent family. It is not yet a C*-completion theorem.\n\n### 4. State transport\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> Pull the target product state back along the algebraic alpha.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nTargetStageStates.targetLimitState\nTargetStageStates.pulledBackState\nTargetStageStates.pulledBackState_eq_targetLimitState_alpha\nTargetStageStates.pulledBackState_isAlgebraicState\n```\n\nSemantic status: the state-level implication is proved from compatible target\nstage states. The infinite product density operator itself is not constructed\nas a von Neumann-algebraic state in this module.\n\n### 5. Algebraic operator representation\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> Compatible finite-stage operator representations define a representation of\n> the quasi-local algebra.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nalgebraicLimitOperatorRep\nalgebraicLimitOperatorRep_of\nalgebraicLimitOperatorRep_stage_congr\nalgebraicLimitOperatorRep_injective\n```\n\nSemantic status: proved conditionally. Injectivity requires stagewise\ninjectivity; no infinite tensor-product Hilbert space is constructed.\n\n### 6. Concrete C*-model\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> Complete the quasi-local algebra in the operator norm.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nOperatorRepresentation.rangeClosure\nOperatorRepresentation.embedding\nOperatorRepresentation.denseRange_embedding\n```\n\nand, for the direct-limit range,\n\n```lean\nquasilocalCStarAlgebra\nquasilocalEmbedding\ndenseRange_quasilocalEmbedding\n```\n\nSemantic status: the closure is genuinely constructed inside bounded\noperators, but only after an isometric operator representation is supplied.\nThis does not prove that the manuscript's algebra has such a representation.\n\n### 7. State-preserving GNS transport\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> A state-preserving C*-isomorphism induces a canonical GNS unitary.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nStatePreservingData.sourceState_eq_pullback\nStatePreservingData.gnsUnitary\nStatePreservingData.gnsUnitary_intertwines\nStatePreservingData.gnsConjStarAlgEquiv\n```\n\nSemantic status: proved from supplied C*-completions, state positivity/order\ndata, continuity, and an exact state identity. It is not a proof of the\nmanuscript's state identity.\n\n### 8. Bicommutant transport\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> The GNS unitary identifies the represented von Neumann algebras.\n\nLean anchors:\n\n```lean\nStarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated\nStarSubalgebra.le_vonNeumannGenerated\nStarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated_le\nbicommutantStarEquiv_sourceRepVN\n```\n\nSemantic status: the algebraic bicommutant/conjugation statement is proved.\nThe identification with strong/weak operator closure and the normal-folium\nstep are conditional interfaces, not proved analytic theorems.\n\n### 9. Product-factor and trace conclusion\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> The product GNS algebra is a type-I pure factor tensor a finite type-I or\n> hyperfinite type-II1 mixed factor, with the appropriate trace conclusion.\n\nLean anchors:\n\n```lean cddddddddssssssssssssssssssssssssssw1\nProductGNSFactorization.pureFactor_typeI_of_finite\nProductGNSFactorization.pureFactor_typeIInfinity_of_infinite\nProductGNSFactorization.mixedFactor_typeI_of_finite\nProductGNSFactorization.mixedFactor_hyperfiniteII1_of_infinite\nfinitePureSector_product_classification\ninfinitePureSector_product_classification\n```\n\nSemantic status: the type labels and tensor identification are supplied data.\nThe finite algebraic trace transport is proved. The infinite-pure package does\nnot yet provide a faithful normal semifinite weight, so the corrected\ninfinite-sector trace conclusion is not formalized.\n\n--- decision tail ---\n# Formalization semantic-audit decision\n\nDate: 2026-08-07\n\nThe approved deliverable is a semantic audit/tutorial of the Lean\nformalization, rather than another proof package or a compilation report.\n\nThe audit will provide:\n\n1. a status summary separating proved mathematics, conditional interfaces,\n   supplied data, and unformalized claims;\n2. a dependency map from the manuscript's finite-coordinate argument through\n   the algebraic limit, concrete C-star model, GNS transport, bicommutant\n   transport, and product-factor boundary;\n3. a theorem ledger mapping each important natural-language proof sentence to\n   exact Lean declarations, hypotheses, intermediate lemmas, and semantic\n   verdicts; and\n4. a step-by-step Lean reading sequence with code excerpts and direct build or\n   `#check` commands.\n\nThe audit must keep compilation separate from mathematical validity and must\nidentify exact manuscript locators from `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`. In particular,\nit must not call the regional hyperfinite-factor theorem proved merely because\nconditional Lean interfaces compile.\n\nThe first pass will inventory the current modules and completed-package\nreviews. Later passes will inspect the principal declarations and their proof\nchains in dependency order.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
